Create the file exclusively in the Windows mkstemp().
mkstemp() chose a name with mktemp() and then opened it with O_CREAT
but without O_EXCL. A file that another process created under that
name in between was opened and shared instead of causing a failure, so
the caller lost the guarantee that the file is new and its own. Add
O_EXCL, so that mkstemp() fails with EEXIST instead.

---
 win32/mingw.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1138,7 +1138,7 @@
 	char *filename = mktemp(template);
 	if (filename == NULL)
 		return -1;
-	return open(filename, O_RDWR | O_CREAT, 0600);
+	return open(filename, O_RDWR | O_CREAT | O_EXCL, 0600);
 }
 
 int gettimeofday(struct timeval *tv, void *tz UNUSED_PARAM)
